{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>אי.</b> When he mentioned the matter of the fool — that he is a dullard — he said: if this one were a king, it would be a harsh thing, all the more so if he were also a youth. And the word אי is like אוי, like ואי לו האחד שיפול, and they have no third in their matter." "<b>ושריך בבקר יאכלו.</b> Because they engage in nothing but eating, he set the time for judgment in the morning."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:00.469162627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}